{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"inferior-mystical-arrowworm","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/unit cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_lock_holder_labelling.py:1-11` — Preserve diagnostic identification of lock holders. Consumer: concurrency maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_lock_retry_zebrafish.py:1-13` — Preserve bounded lock acquisition retry behavior. Consumer: concurrency maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py:84-89, 166-175, 213-217, 267-272` — Preserve stale detection, live-owner protection, and reclaim atomicity. Consumer: concurrency maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_lock_timeout_names_holder_7084.py:1-12` — Preserve timeout diagnostics naming the current holder. Consumer: concurrency maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_main_health_report.py:1-11` — Preserve main-health report schema and status semantics. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_make_lint_hygiene_wiring.py:1-9` — Preserve hygiene checks wired into make lint. Consumer: build maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_marker_single_emission_f829.py:1-16` — Preserve exactly-once marker emission. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_max_tokens_model_ceiling_1019.py:1-33` — Preserve model ceiling enforcement and safe max-token clamping. Consumer: LLM-runtime maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py:1-16, 87-92, 296-304, 378-387, 470-481, 511-525, 561-574, 659-675, 705-717, 737-749, 794-812` — Preserve entrypoint provisioning, environment propagation, failure diagnostics, and idempotence. Consumer: MCP deployment maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py:233-237, 286-290, 443-448, 502-506, 603-606, 626-628` — Preserve deduplication, durable job-state transitions, sidecar readiness, and error behavior. Consumer: MCP gate maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_unreadable_config_errors_8408.py:1-10` — Preserve actionable errors for unreadable gate configuration. Consumer: MCP maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_health_startup_handshake.py:1-23, 402-408` — Preserve readiness handshake ordering and startup-failure diagnostics. Consumer: MCP deployment maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_health_store_status.py:1-17, 96-107, 120-127, 177-189` — Preserve health-status distinctions for available, stale, and failing stores. Consumer: MCP maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_inflight.py:1-18` — Preserve same-key operation deduplication and cleanup. Consumer: MCP gate maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_library_parity.py:1-21, 199-208` — Preserve MCP-to-library operation and schema parity. Consumer: MCP API maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_llm_dedup.py:1-9, 65-71` — Preserve single execution for concurrent equivalent LLM operations. Consumer: MCP gate maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py:269-285, 324-333, 457-504, 539-557, 787-837, 873-1091, 1104-1327` — Preserve trust-boundary, credential, signing-key, service-hardening, deployment-order, and rollback invariants. Consumer: security and MCP deployment maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py:1-23` — Preserve on-box operation-certificate signing and trust binding. Consumer: security and MCP maintainers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_lock_holder_labelling.py tests/unit/test_lock_retry_zebrafish.py tests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py tests/unit/test_lock_timeout_names_holder_7084.py tests/unit/test_main_health_report.py tests/unit/test_make_lint_hygiene_wiring.py tests/unit/test_marker_single_emission_f829.py tests/unit/test_max_tokens_model_ceiling_1019.py tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_unreadable_config_errors_8408.py tests/unit/test_mcp_health_startup_handshake.py tests/unit/test_mcp_health_store_status.py tests/unit/test_mcp_inflight.py tests/unit/test_mcp_library_parity.py tests/unit/test_mcp_llm_dedup.py tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py tests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","id":"aa30-0d85-40e9-44e1","parent_id":"ae4d-df34-480d-4c88","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in tests/unit — cohort 17: lock_holder_labelling–mcp_opcert_signing_goose"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREAT